Our project showcases a recipe program where a user can explore recipes made by others and upload their own as well. We decided to implement these using page navigation, input fields, and grid layouts. We implemented a featured recipes section on our homescreen and made sure each page was navigatible from every other page. Since we aren't using javascript for this project, none of the submit/add to list buttons work in the form sections of our program, meaning you cannot actually create your own recipe. What we have showcased is what it would look like if you were able to submit your own recipe. Grid layout was used for spacing recipe cards, and each section of every page was divided by divs to keep organization. We kept all of our css on one style sheet to keep consistent styles throughout each page and for good code organization.